# Nothing proves that `first` is whole, so `value` is a number. The remainder of a whole dividend is taken of integers, and that integer goes round the loop in a Phi of its own.
# While it is known and at most 2^48, the product and the sum are those of integers too: no conversion lies on the way from one remainder to the next.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="scrambled" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[carried]] = Phi(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[isKnown]] = BelowEqual(b@[[carried]], $281474976710656(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:Mod)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isKnown]], Terminal, {{*}}:Mod)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[product]] = Mul(b@[[carried]], $31(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:Mod)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[sum]] = Add(b@[[product]], $7(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:Mod)
# CHECK-NEXT: Upsilon(b@[[sum]], ^[[dividend]],
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[dividend]] = Phi(
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[remainder]] = Sub(b@[[dividend]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Mod)
# CHECK: Upsilon(b@[[remainder]], ^
# Where the integer is not known the number is tested as ever, and the remainder of a fraction leaves it unknown.
# CHECK: Double b@[[numberProduct]] = Mul(b@{{*}}:Mul)
# CHECK: Double b@[[numberSum]] = Add(b@[[numberProduct]], {{*}}:Add)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@{{*}} = Patchpoint(b@[[numberSum]]:SomeRegister,
# CHECK: Upsilon($-1(b@{{*}}), ^
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function

# Half a degree is added each time round, so the sum is whole at most every other time: the angle is carried as a number alone.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="turned" role=Source
# CHECK-NOT: Int64 b@{{*}} = Phi(
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
